# Acervator — .gitignore
# Added 2026-08-05 with cascade C00 (baseline snapshot protocol).
# Principle: ignore only what is regenerable, transient, or oversized.
# Everything else is tracked, because C00 exists to make rollback real
# and a rollback that omits files is not a rollback.
#
# NOTE: _archive/ and .session26_backups/ ARE tracked on purpose —
# cascade C43 and others restore archived pin tests out of them.

# ── Python bytecode / build ─────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ── Build + distribution artefacts (71 MB, fully regenerable) ───
build/
dist/
*.manifest

# ── Tool caches ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
.deepeval/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# ── Runtime logs ────────────────────────────────────────────────
_logs/
*.log

# ── Gate artefact ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generated by tools/harness/check_release_readiness.py on every run.
# Tracking it would let a stale green sidecar ride into a commit.
.release_ready.json

# ── Oversized transient captures ────────────────────────────────
# 63 MB conversation-transcript backup; not source.
ACERVATOR_DEV_1_BACKUP_*.jsonl
pytest_out.txt
pytest_v3_*.txt

# ── Agent scratch ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Worktrees created for isolated agent runs. 1,414 files / ~30 MB were
# landing in the release zip before this rule; they are scratch, not
# project content.
.claude/worktrees/

# ── OS / editor noise ───────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~

# ── NEVER TRACK ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The operator's live runtime tree lives at ~/.acervator/ and
# ~/.acervator_logs/, outside this repo, and must stay outside it.
# These patterns are a backstop in case a copy is ever made here.
**/coinbase_credentials.json
**/bot_state.json
**/bot_state.backup.json
**/reservation_state.json
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*

# SADP deprecated 2026-08 - session backstop diffs, 71 MB, regenerable
.sadp/

# Written by tools/gate.py. Records WHICH COMMIT the gate proved, for the
# pre-push hook. Never commit it: it is per-clone and committing it would
# change the very sha it certifies.
.gate_stamp.json

# ── Per-clone harness state (regenerated at runtime) ────────────
# The touchset pin and island ledger both record an ABSOLUTE machine
# root (like .gate_stamp.json above). Committing them baked one Windows
# user's path into the repo; they are per-clone state, not source, and
# tools/touchset.py + tools/island.py rewrite them on the next run.
tools/.touchset_pin.json
tools/.island_ledger.jsonl

# ── Local Claude Code settings (per-user, incl. backups) ────────
# settings.local.json is personal, and *.pre_consolidation_* etc. are
# transient snapshots of it. Only settings.json is shared.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/settings.local.json.*
